  "highlights": [
    "Limit, market, IOC, FOK, post-only, cancel and cancel/replace with correct priority rules (size-down keeps priority; size-up or reprice loses it)",
    "Self-trade prevention (cancel newest), gap-free sequence numbers on every ack, fill, cancel, reject and L2 increment",
    "Hypothesis property tests: never crossed, quantity conserved, price-time priority, replay and event-sourced rebuild produce identical book hashes",
    "Backtester trades through the real engine: queue position, latency, fees, slippage, and an exact integer PnL decomposition (mid / spread / fees)"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Pure Python: 214,338 orders/s and tens of µs tail latency on a laptop, not the millions/s and sub-µs of a C++/Rust engine on a pinned core",
    "Synthetic market: background participants are stylised, so strategy PnL shows mechanics and cost sensitivity, not tradeable alpha",
    "Single instrument, no auctions, halts, or iceberg/hidden orders"
